SQLite for OpenVMS (vms-sqlite)
===============================

SQLite is in the public domain. Its authors' dedication
(https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html):

  The author disclaims copyright to this source code. In place of a legal
  notice, here is a blessing:

     May you do good and not evil.
     May you find forgiveness for yourself and forgive others.
     May you share freely, never taking more than you give.

  Anyone is free to copy, modify, publish, use, compile, sell, or distribute
  the original SQLite code, either in source code form or as a compiled
  binary, for any purpose, commercial or non-commercial, and by any means.

This repository's own files (the OpenVMS VFS in overlay/vmsport, the patches in
patches/, the build and test procedures, the tools and the documentation) are
dedicated to the public domain in the same way: anyone is free to copy,
modify, publish, use, compile, sell, or distribute them, in source or binary
form, for any purpose, commercial or non-commercial, and by any means. They are
provided as is, without warranty of any kind.
